    -- **`{endpoint-asset-ingestion,endpoint-gateway-ingestion,scanner-event-consumer,mcp-gateway-event-consumer}.enabled:
    -  false` — keep all four, and add one for any new AWS-only lane whose shared overlay gets registered.** The chart
    +- **`endpoint-asset-ingestion` is now ENABLED here, and it is the one exception to the rule below.** The MCP
    +  scanner lane has an Azure implementation (Blob → Event Grid → Service Bus → the in-process writer), so this
    +  instance sets `enabled: true` and supplies the lane's own `asset_ingestion_asb` stanza. Three traps come with it:
    +  - **The lane binds its OWN published keys — `${endpoint_asset_ingestion_servicebus_namespace}` and
    +    `${endpoint_asset_ingestion_queue_name}` — never the shared `${servicebus_namespace}`.** The shared key is
    +    published only when the *extension* lane's toggle is on, so reusing it would make this lane silently depend
    +    on a different lane's switch.
    +  - **Those two keys are published CONDITIONALLY** (`cell-azure-instance/fluxcd_config.tf`, gated on
    +    `create_service_bus && var.create_endpoint_asset_ingestion_queue`), and Flux resolves an unprovided `${...}`
    +    to the **empty string** while the Kustomization still reconciles. Enabling this lane on an instance whose
    +    queue toggle is off therefore renders an empty queue name and fails at the POD — the transport guard refuses
    +    to start, a CrashLoopBackOff — not at the render. **Apply infrastructure first, then this toggle.**
    +  - **`asset_ingestion_s3.{aws_region,endpoint}` are blanked HERE, not in `drop-aws-only-values.yaml`.** Removing
    +    a key from `spec.values` does not stop the chart's default reappearing, and that default is a live
    +    `aws_region: us-east-1`. Because the drop file is patched *after* this one, a remove there would delete the
    +    blanks set here — so this leaf is blanked in place and deliberately absent from the drop list.
    +
    +- **`{endpoint-gateway-ingestion,scanner-event-consumer,mcp-gateway-event-consumer}.enabled:
    +  false` — keep all three, and add one for any new AWS-only lane whose shared overlay gets registered.** The chart
