    -  to `true`, so the instance disable is what wins. Enabled on Azure, their `${...:=}` queue URLs render empty and
    -  their region renders the published `us-east-1`, giving workloads that start and consume nothing.
    +  to `true`, so the instance disable is what wins. Enabled on Azure *without* an Azure transport, their
    +  `${...:=}` queue URLs render empty and their region renders the published `us-east-1`, giving workloads that
    +  start and consume nothing — which is precisely the failure the `endpoint-asset-ingestion` entry above avoids by
    +  supplying a real Azure transport rather than merely flipping the toggle.
     
